use you look  at schwartz he missed over half the  season with the back injury and they  kept talking about well maybe he can  come back maybe he might be able to come  back for the super bowl that didn't  happen eric fisher tears his achilles  during the afc championship game so who  even knows when he's going to be  available to play if he's going to be  able available to play in 2021 so i  think you know a few weeks ago mike we  were saying on this show hey man the  chiefs have got to be able to shore up  their backup situation and in this  particular case i almost feel like well  they're just saying let's rip the  band-aid off let's just go with the  whole rebuild of our offensive line  because frankly we won't necessarily be  able to rely on both of these guys for  being healthy in 2021 and as long as  we've got patrick mahomes we know that  our window is wide open so if that's the  case then let's just try to rebuild our  offensive line entirely i guess that's  just the approach they're taking what's  going to happen this offseason and  what's already happening now it's not  something that is unusual in that  it doesn't occur just doesn't occur to  this extent but it underscores the fact  that these football players on every  team are interchangeable parts now some  are more interchangeable than others  punters kickers it's very easy to say  we're removing one we're adding another  one because that person's performance  isn't dependent in any way on those  around him but even the guys like an  offensive line where ideally it works  five guys  in sync  even then even then  all of these players are  pieces of a machine  and at some point that piece gets  removed and a new piece gets put in  and they're constantly looking  for new pieces that would be cheaper and  or more effective than the pieces they  currently have that's what they do we've  talked about that before that jarring i  said magnets on the board you pointed  out it's actually all digital now but  however they do it  they're always looking they always have  the list of 10 left tackles 10 right  tackles 10 quarterbacks 10 guys at every  position that they would call if they  need someone and they have people who  are working behind the scenes to come up  with those lists studying film analyzing  contractual expectations  and this year more than any other miles  with all of these veterans out there who  will be available potentially at a  bargain basement price you're going to  have teams looking at their roster  looking at who's available and saying  hmm you know we've had this guy on the  team for eight years he's a great leader  he's a great part of the community but  the bottom line is dollar for dollar i  can get better value from one of these  veterans that was cut by another team so  i'm gonna do it and it's it's cold it's  dispassionate it is anything but  football is family  but  it shows you how the family business of  a football operation works guys get  ushered out the door all the time  with  if they're lucky  a social media graphic that says thank  you well and i think that what you were  pointing out earlier about the fact that  the cap is actually about 25 million  dollars lower than it was expected to be  in 2021 not just that it dropped from  last year that expectation is how teams  set up their their teams for years down  the road so if a team right now is  almost 20 million dollars over the cap  that means that they were not expecting  to be over the cap by that much or at  all at this point um in 2021 so  that i think has a lot to do with the  way teams are going to be constructed  for this upcoming season i think it's  going to be weird i think some guys who  are veterans are going to say you know  what just pay me a little bit and just  let me on this team and maybe we'll go  win a championship and i'll bet on  myself for the next year other teams  might just take the approach of we're  going to have a bunch of undrafted  rookies in here because i think about  the falcons and their team that does not  have that many contracts that they can  restructure they've got a quarterback  and a wide receiver who are very highly  paid they don't really have anybody that  many people on the roster right now  either so you're gonna have to probably  usher in a bunch of low paid veterans  and probably a bunch of undrafted free  agents and say hey man let's just get  out there and let's see what happens  let's see how good our coaching is let's  see how good our scouting department is  and let's just see what these guys can  do and that i think is going to happen  all over the league between the good  teams and the bad teams good teams  probably going to want these cheap  veterans bad teams to say let's just be  bad for this year and let's just weather  the storm and maybe in 2022 things will  be better  social media gives us plenty of bad  things it also gives us some good things  like footage from the future exclusive  footage of patrick mahomes  next season  lining up for the  kansas city chiefs that's kind of what  it was like in super bowl 55 and they  can't do much worse and part of it was  on them too 92 i think of the snaps were  just five guys  the five offensive linemen with no help  against that buccaneers defense so maybe  that maybe they'll keep a tight end in  once in a while or running back in once  in a while to help block for patrick  mahomes next year  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

